    "goal": "Plan a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives, followup f-asrswtwl-live-worker-read-dead: establish whether a watcher still reads a live worker as dead with retained work at current main, before any repair. Read the followup in docs/plans/a-stalled-row-says-whether-the-worker-lives.html. On 2026-09-25 the follower emitted the dead-pid-with-retained-work interruption for two runs whose supervisors plus workers were alive with fresh streams, while the MCP live view classified both running; the watcher process had been running since before several liveness changes. From the code at HEAD, name the exact condition that emits that interruption (reckon/crew/recovery.py, requires process_alive False), each input it reads, then determine whether any path still lets a live process read as not alive: a stale watcher process holding old code, a pid read from the wrong record, a host mismatch, or a start-time check. State whether the defect reproduces at HEAD, with file:line evidence read from git show HEAD, plus the minimal repair if it does.",
